# CTF-01 whole-method explicit-member Native helper proposal

SOURCE ONLY. This package has not been imported, configured, compiled or run.
It adds a small caller and metadata serializer around the separately held full
derived Construction translation unit. The original tree and cached archive are
unchanged. Root must freeze the literal inputs, projection and variable precision
before any actual Native call. There is no new source-review execution stage.

The request/admission/projection/result schemas are `ctf01-helper-cases.v1`,
`ctf01-native-admission-contract.v1`, `ctf01-observation-projection.v1`, and
`ctf01-helper-results.v1`. Runtime argv is exactly:

```
ctf01_reference_helper <repository-root> <frozen-request> <native-admission-contract> <fresh-output-directory>
```

The request contains input-only `contracts: {source,tolerances}`; admission adds
the cases contract, projection and exact seven Native code files. Cases binds the
request/source/tolerances/fixed CON15/all45 guards. Projection binds request and
all three contracts. No contract points forward to results, compiled hashes or a
future receipt. The source-only input authority is the held input-design-prep-01;
its 39 models/42 calls are proposed arrays, not hardcoded actual helper counts.
Request/admission also bind the genuine runtime-supplied scope amendment and its
actual execution receipt by identical path/SHA, without guessing future identities.

Each model has the agreed six exact operand keys and the `explicit-member-unit`
lane. Scalar inputs are finite, exact `{bits:16-lowercase-hex}` DTOs. NoMass-form
members are genuine positive-zero d/k/rho/cp with positive literal stored R;
ordinary massive members are positive. Ordered membership/call indices are
bounded to the actual eleven-layer capacity. Source/sink and two-dimensional
branches remain excluded. `Resistance` is copied as supplied; no d/k expression
or loader is called by the wrapper. MaterialBase's constructor group is replaced
by the explicitly selected actual Regular group for both forms. Other unselected
members retain their real constructor defaults and are not claimed as loader data.

A fresh real EnergyPlusData is constructed and init_constant_state is called per
model. Both real owner arrays are allocated before any whole call. Every material
is a MaterialBase owned by MaterialData; every construction is an actual Construct
array element. LayerPoint contains the real material indices, and the output
retains logical IDs, actual array indices/Num/names and original membership/order.
The stable construction address is the real identity used by the unchanged
downstream reverse-construction scan. Shared ErrorsFound/DoCTFErrorReport bools
are initialized once per model and passed by reference in declared array order.
ErrorsFound=true does not make the wrapper skip a subsequent call. Teardown calls
MaterialData::clear_state exactly once because EnergyPlusData's default destructor
does not delete its raw material pointees. No double-owned temporary is retained.

Each actual whole calculateTransferFunction call has before/after public-owner
snapshots, real diagnostic offsets and the held three-phase passive Capture.
PostLoad/PostMerge emit no dyn/rs/cnd operands; PostConversion copies those actual
initialized locals. Only the reached active prefix is serialized. Unreached
checkpoints are unavailable, not zero arrays. IsUsedCTF=false and real early-return
branches therefore receive no invented observations. The entire original method
continues after the last callback; no prefix formula or early stop is substituted.
Later coefficients, solver flags and thermal behavior are context-only/unpaired.

Actual FatalError, std::exception (actual RTTI/message), nonstandard exception and
normal return are separate outcomes. A returned method is not a scientific PASS;
its actual error flags remain observed. After a caught constructor/init/source
exception, remaining calls are explicitly not invoked, with unknown source
fatal/exception fields and null Capture. An OS crash cannot be caught or turned
into method records: the actual process exit and absent/incomplete output must be
retained by a future launcher. This source does not infer those process outcomes.

Observer integrity flags are separate from source outcomes. Binding/identity/
duplicate/order/prefix failure never changes or short-circuits the genuine call.
After all records are written, exit2 means an actual observer integrity failure;
exit0 means the requested record ledger was written, not all phases or science
passed. Wrapper admission/I/O errors return1. Logs are actual err/audit/eso/eio
streams and callback messages. No expected diagnostics/exits are supplied.

The CMake proposal includes the unchanged SCH05 adapter, preserving existing661
command registrations. It adds three new executable source objects: helper,
full instrumented Construction, and callback. They precede unchanged energypluslib
in the normal executable link. No cached original Construction object is replaced,
no archive is modified, and no whole-archive option is used. Definitions/includes
come from the genuine core target/directory and the same project option targets.
A real future link map must prove the derived object supplied the Construction
symbols and the original Construction archive member was not selected. Counts,
flags, object paths, protected artifacts and linker providers require actual build
inspection; this package claims no compiled provenance or protected-byte check.
The adapter takes explicit CTF01_HELPER_SOURCE_DIR/CTF01_OBSERVER_SOURCE_DIR and
CLK03_REPOSITORY_ROOT, so reviewed canonical copies can be used without changing
these held sources. Cached643 core objects/original sources remain protected.

Fixed CON15/all45 bindings are preservation guards only for this unit helper.
The later production lane requires genuine InputProcessor/Material/construction
loaders and actual CTF-use owners. These literal seeds cannot certify that path.
CTF02 through CTF10 and all thermal coefficient/results remain unclaimed. No
canonical edit, engine, project import, compiler, formatter, Git, scientific
result or binary read was performed while authoring this source proposal.
